# vercel.json sets outputDirectory to ".", so the whole project directory becomes the
# static output. Deploys triggered from git only ever contain committed files, and
# .claude/worktrees is gitignored, so production is unaffected — this file covers the
# local `vercel deploy` path, which uploads the working directory as-is and would
# otherwise publish a stale duplicate of the site from an agent worktree.
#
# Note: this does NOT filter `vercel build --prebuilt` output, which copies the working
# directory after the build. Run local Vercel builds from a clean checkout.
#
# Do NOT add src/, scripts/, package.json or api/ here: the build reads the first three
# and api/ is what Vercel compiles into the serverless functions.
.claude
